+# G2: bounded producer/plan and arena validation
+
+This is executable GPU test authoring, not a GPU result. Execution must remain within Daniel's applicable authorization; this authoring
+work performs no execution or lifecycle action. Frozen deployment 610cbde remains unchanged.
+
+## Boundary
+
+`test_deepseek_v41_q03_owner.py` invokes the real legal mHC `post_pre` producer:
+BF16 x/residual, previous post/comb, norm and pre tensors are supplied. Its
+explicit arena q/sf outputs feed the real `MoeExpertsV41Plan.run`. Nothing
+replaces the producer or consumer with FakeTensor or mock arithmetic. A
+counting wrapper delegates to the real input cast and checks one baseline cast
+versus zero dual casts. The comparator is the candidate's BF16 path, NOT the
+original 188 implementation; original-188 numerical proof belongs to G1.
+
+The fixture preserves H=5120 and per-rank I=576; it bounds expert count to 8,
+top-k to 2, active rows to 96. It never constructs a model or loads checkpoint
+weights. Before tensors are constructed, its conservative payload estimate is
+275,775,488 bytes (four times packed weights plus 128 MiB), under a 512 MiB
+payload budget. It separately requires 2 GiB free device memory. Neither value
+is a measured peak or a bound on compiler/driver allocations. Each test owns a
+fresh function-scoped fixture and current vLLM configuration.
+
+Twelve selected cases cover:
+- nine row/steering combinations (1/16/96, off/loaded-zero/active);
+- a real deferred shared addend with CUDA event ordering and independent cast
+  verification of the surviving arena q/sf;
+- three real captured shapes alternating replay with eager execution, changed
+  inputs/doses, poisoned unused capacity, and stable owner storage pointers;
+- graph-resource retention after the Python owner is dropped.
+
+The two arena allocations total 43,253,760 bytes at capacity 8192. Only up to 96
+rows run through the actual producer/plan here. Byte equality is deliberately
+strict; any mismatch stops the gate and requires investigation, not tolerance
+relaxation. CUDA synchronizations and `.item()` calls occur in assertions,
+not runtime model changes.
+
+## Invocation and stop conditions
+
+Once applicable GPU authorization is verified, run from the candidate checkout with its
+approved installed runtime and dependency set (do not overlay source through
+PYTHONPATH). Record `vllm.__file__`, component/runtime identity, CUDA/device
+identity, command, collected count and full result in the run manifest first.
+The packaging/P0 gate is responsible for proving those identities.
+
+```
+VLLM_Q03_RUN_G2_GPU=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q \
+  tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_q03_owner.py
+```
+
+Expected selected count: 12, all must pass. Without opt-in the module skips
+before Torch/runtime imports. A default skip is NOT success. With opt-in,
+missing dependencies, non-SM121, insufficient memory, compilation errors,
+zero collection, skips, numerical differences or alias/lifetime failures are
+stop conditions. Do not install, restart, deploy or repair hardware as a side
+effect of this command. The pure `_gpu_requested(environ)` helper can be
+AST-extracted by a stdlib selection test without Torch imports.
+
+## Explicitly remaining gates
+
+This test does not construct MoERunner, the production shared expert, a TP4
+model or a drafter. Its shared addend tests the plan's callable/event boundary,
+not production runner auxiliary-stream scheduling. The owner is borrowed by
+eager Python during capture, not by `torch.compile(fullgraph=True)` model
+execution. The test manually retains the graph-resource collector list; it
+does not prove production graph-wrapper retirement/lifetime behavior.
+
+A full-model gate still needs approved TP4 checkpoint/distributed fixtures,
+actual startup allocation accounting and guards (target/non-SP/TP4/SM121,
+draft/SP/unsupported/capacity baseline), actual production graph wrappers,
+fullgraph compilation and sequential layer/graph ownership. Exercise real
+capacity boundaries including 8192, all steering modes, candidate off/on,
+production shared-expert event ordering, and alternating eager/captured
+requests. Concurrent graph replays on independent streams are outside the
+single-slot contract and must not be presented as supported.
+
+Stage execution: P0 installed imports/opaque LayerName, G1 original188/BF16/dual,
+then this bounded G2, then the separately prepared TP4 full-model gate. Stop at
+first failure. Candidate remains off by default. Rollback is startup with
+VLLM_DS41_Q03_MHC_MXFP8 unset or 0, through an authorized restart;
+no service command is part of this test or cloud authoring work.
